    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d795">

                <pb facs="0738" n="566" sameAs="frus:frus1917Supp01v01/pg566"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72111/5063a</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Assistant Secretary of State</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Phillips</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Assistant
                        Secretary of the Treasury</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Peters</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-02-10">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">February 10, 1917</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Mr. Peters</hi>: The Secretaries of the British and French
                    Embassies called upon me yesterday requesting that steps be taken so that the
                    publication of manifests of ships sailing from the United States for Allied
                    countries be discontinued.</p>
                <p>I merely desire to bring these facts to your attention and to inquire whether, in
                    your opinion, it would be possible to take any steps looking to the
                    discontinuance of the publication of the manifests.</p>
                <p>Sincerely yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">William Phillips</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
